cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DexVantage in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DexVantage: camera, depth and teleop planning for robot-learning data collection"
abstract: >-
  DexVantage is a desktop application for planning and checking the camera, depth and tactile sensing of robot
  manipulation and humanoid data-collection rigs: where cameras go so fingertips, objects and contacts stay visible at
  the grasp, where depth is valid, what the teleoperator can reach, and whether recorded datasets meet the plan.
authors:
  - name: "Sherin Joseph Roy"
    website: "https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI"
version: "0.1.0.dev0"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sherin-SEF-AI/DexVantage"
keywords:
  - robot learning
  - manipulation
  - camera placement
  - hand-eye calibration
  - data collection
  - LeRobot
